# SYNTHETIC: the census, every chat reply, the system alerts and the
# profile replies below were made up for the offline chat checks on planet
# 1801 (Slag): the room list, entries, room information, chat lines, leaving
# and creating rooms, the server's echo of a line said to the room, a page
# (system_alert type 2) and a ticker line (type 0), and the profile_info and
# ladder_profile replies to a get_profile for another player in the room.
#
# Rover replies for an offline login to CorePrime Alpha replayed by
# open-annihilation --boneyards-replay for the chat checks and by the Boneyards client tests.
# The login, dossier, area_name, allegiance, census and activity lines are
# those of alpha_planets.replay: user id 1 is oa_check, a Core commander.

# Contact, clearance, then login_confirmed for user id 1.
progress 4 0 0 0
progress 7 0 0 0
progress 8 0 1 0

delay 2
dossier USER_STATUS int 1
dossier LOGINNAME string oa_check
dossier ALLEGIANCE string C

area_name alpha

# SYNTHETIC: a news ticker line after the login.
# alert KIND TEXT[|NOTIFICATION_TYPE]
alert 0 Slag is under siege: every commander to the front lines

delay 1
allegiances CCCCIIIAAACCCCCCAAAAAAAAC

# SYNTHETIC: the census and activity lines below were made up for the
# checks; every planet has a nonzero population and the contested planets
# (1800-1802 by the allegiance line) have wins.
# census AREA POPULATION ACTIVITY IN_PROGRESS FORMING CORE_WINS ARM_WINS
census 1796 12 1 0 1 0 0
census 1797 7 0 0 0 0 0
census 1798 5 1 1 0 0 0
census 1799 9 0 0 0 0 0
census 1800 21 2 1 1 3 4
census 1801 34 3 2 1 17 9
census 1802 16 1 0 2 6 11
census 1803 8 0 0 0 0 0
census 1804 4 1 0 1 0 0
census 1805 11 0 0 0 0 0
census 1806 6 0 0 0 0 0
census 1807 3 1 1 0 0 0
census 1808 2 0 0 0 0 0
census 1809 5 0 0 0 0 0
census 1810 8 2 1 1 0 0
census 1811 4 0 0 0 0 0
census 1812 10 1 0 1 0 0
census 1813 3 0 0 0 0 0
census 1814 7 0 0 0 0 0
census 1815 2 1 1 0 0 0
census 1816 6 0 0 0 0 0
census 1817 9 2 1 1 0 0
census 1818 1 0 0 0 0 0
census 1819 5 0 0 0 0 0
census 1820 13 1 0 1 0 0
activity 1010231010010020100102001

# Slag's frequencies: two planetary defaults (type 1), a user-created one
# (type 3) that needs a password and names its creator as its tag, and a
# battle debriefing (type 2). Each lists the users in it before the check
# user arrives.
delay 1
# room AREA ROOM USERS TYPE NEEDS_PW NAME|DESCRIPTION|TAG
room 1801 1 1 1 0 Main|Planetary default frequency
room 1801 2 1 1 0 Staging Area|Planetary default frequency
room 1801 3 2 3 1 Clan Hall|Clan members only|Ghost_Commander
room 1801 4 0 2 0 Debriefing|Battle debriefing
# DP Alpha's one frequency, for switching planets.
room 1796 1 1 1 0 Main|Planetary default frequency

# Entering either default brings its members, a server notice and a line
# from the second user, then a room-list update counting the check user in.
# The check user is refused the user-created frequency.
# entered AREA ROOM RESULT
entered 1801 1 0
update 0 1801 1 2 1 0 Main|Planetary default frequency
# SYNTHETIC: Ghost_Commander pages the check user once either default is
# entered.
# page USER_ID TEXT
page 7 <Page from Ghost_Commander> Meet me in the Clan Hall
entered 1801 2 0
update 0 1801 2 2 1 0 Staging Area|Planetary default frequency
page 7 <Page from Ghost_Commander> Meet me in the Clan Hall
entered 1801 3 1
entered 1796 1 0
update 0 1796 1 2 1 0 Main|Planetary default frequency
# member AREA ROOM USER_ID LATENCY ICON RANK ALLEGIANCE NAME
member 1801 1 1 1 1 0 C oa_check
member 1801 1 7 2 8 0 C Ghost_Commander
member 1801 2 1 1 1 0 C oa_check
member 1801 2 7 2 8 0 C Ghost_Commander
member 1796 1 1 1 1 0 C oa_check
member 1796 1 9 1 17 0 A Dan
# said AREA ROOM USER_ID TEXT (user 0: the server)
said 1801 1 0 Welcome to Slag, commander.
said 1801 1 7 Anyone up for a 1v1 on Acid Pools?
said 1801 2 0 Welcome to Slag, commander.
said 1801 2 7 Anyone up for a 1v1 on Acid Pools?
said 1796 1 9 Quiet out here on DP Alpha.

# Lines said to the room come back from user 1.
echo on

# left AREA ROOM RESULT
left 1801 1 0
left 1801 2 0
left 1796 1 0

# +create Outpost is made as room 5 and entered; Main is taken.
# created AREA ROOM NAME
created 1801 5 Outpost
update 0 1801 5 1 3 0 Outpost||oa_check
entered 1801 5 0
member 1801 5 1 1 1 0 C oa_check
created 0 0 Main

# Forward Base, asked for from the Create Frequency pane with no description
# or password, is made as room 6; the switch into it is answered and the
# list then counts the check user in it, who later leaves.
created 1801 6 Forward Base
update 0 1801 6 1 3 0 Forward Base||oa_check
entered 1801 6 0
update 0 1801 6 1 3 0 Forward Base||oa_check
member 1801 6 1 1 1 0 C oa_check
left 1801 6 0

# +locate Ghost_Commander finds him chatting on Slag.
located Ghost_Commander 1 7 8
located_field area_id uint 1801
located_field room_id uint 1
located_field area_name string Slag
located_field room_name string Main

# SYNTHETIC: Ghost_Commander's profile, as the player pane asks for it:
# a Duel and a Galactic War (Core) standing, then his profile_info.
delay 1
# ladder_profile USER_ID LADDER_ID SUBID KEY int|string VALUE
ladder_profile 7 1 0 RANK string 37
ladder_profile 7 1 0 SCORE string 1642
ladder_profile 7 1 0 WS string 58
ladder_profile 7 1 0 LS string 31
ladder_profile 7 1 0 WP string 65%
ladder_profile 7 1 0 GC string 89
ladder_profile 7 4 2 GC string 24
ladder_profile 7 4 2 SPS string 310
ladder_profile 7 4 2 WS string 15
ladder_profile 7 4 2 LS string 9
ladder_profile 7 4 2 FWP string 62%
# profile USER_ID KEY int|string VALUE
profile 7 LOGINNAME string Ghost_Commander
profile 7 ICON int 8
profile 7 ALLEGIANCE string C
profile 7 USER_STATUS int 1
profile 7 CLAN string Red Dawn
profile 7 TAG string Anyone up for a 1v1 on Acid Pools?
profile 7 HAS_CC string Yes
profile 7 HAS_BT string Yes
profile 7 TAFORUM_ALIAS string ghost
profile 7 NUMPLAYERS string 2
profile 7 PLAYERSKILL string 3
profile 7 ONCOMDEATH string 1
profile 7 FAVORITEMAP string Acid Pools
profile 7 BONETIME string 5210
profile 7 JOINDATE string 1998-11-02
profile 7 AWARD_1 string Slag Defender
